; One wide floor with a platform over each half: the left one high, the
; right one low. Nothing here has to be climbed to get around -- the floor is
; continuous and the only ring-outs are its two open ends -- so the platforms
; are for the pickups on them and for a few more seconds once the lava rises.
;
; Eased for issue #59: the left platform came down 24 px (y 140 -> 164, top
; 172 -> 148 px above the floor), still 36 px higher than the right one's
; 112. Its top was just past what a short weapon can fling to: a headless
; search over input sequences found the sword onto it in 15 of ~560 tries
; before and 35 after, the boomstick from its sixth generation to its first.
; The dagger still cannot reach it (it gets within about 30 px, and tops out
; around 120 px of climb from flat ground); it can reach the right one, and
; lowering the left to that height would have erased the high/low pair.

; Backdrop (issue #117): meadow at dusk.
[node name="Flatlands" type="Node2D"]
